      en: "Moheshkhali LNG Terminal is a floating liquefied natural gas (LNG) regasification facility off the coast of Moheshkhali Island in Cox's Bazar district, Bangladesh. Commissioned in 2018, it has a capacity of 3.75 million tonnes of LNG per year (about 500 million cubic feet of gas per day). The terminal consists of a floating storage and regasification unit (FSRU) and a pipeline to shore. It was built to meet growing gas demand as domestic reserves decline. LNG is primarily imported from Qatar and Oman. The terminal is strategically important for Bangladesh's energy security, enabling gas imports for power generation and industry. A second facility is planned.",
